          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3 Algebraic Methods of Solving a Pair of Linear Equations"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.174,
            0.901,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the previous section, we discussed how to solve a pair of linear equations graphically. The graphical method is not convenient in cases when the point representing the solution of the linear equations has non-integral coordinates like",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\sqrt { 3 } }   ,   2 { \\sqrt { 7 } } \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-1.75,3.3),\\left(\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{1}{19}\\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , etc. There is every possibility of making mistakes while reading such coordinates. Is there any alternative method of finding the solution? There are several algebraic methods, which we shall now discuss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.353,
            0.902,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3.1 Substitution Method : We shall explain the method of substitution by taking some examples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.406,
            0.802,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4 : Solve the following pair of equations by substitution method:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.381,
            0.431,
            0.898,
            0.451
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "7 x - 1 5 y = 2\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.456,
            0.897,
            0.476
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "x + 2y = 3\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.482,
            0.205,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.507,
            0.899,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 1 : We pick either of the equations and write one variable in terms of the other. Let us consider the Equation (2) :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.582,
            0.242,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and write it as",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.556,
            0.898,
            0.601
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}x + 2y &= 3 \\\\x &= 3 \\geq 2y\\end{aligned}\\tag{3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.607,
            0.645,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 2 : Substitute the value of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " x "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in Equation (1). We get",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.658,
            0.139,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.684,
            0.139,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.632,
            0.537,
            0.702
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}7(3 - 2y) - 15y &= 2 \\\\21 - 14y - 15y &= 2 \\\\\\angle \\quad - 29y &= - 19\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.723,
            0.205,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.711,
            0.533,
            0.75
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "y = { \\frac { 1 9 } { 2 9 } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.755,
            0.659,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Step 3 : Substituting this value of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " y "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in Equation (3), we get",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.784,
            0.667,
            0.828
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "x = 3 - 2\\left(\\frac{19}{29}\\right) = \\frac{49}{29}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.827,
            0.51,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the solution is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = \\frac { 4 9 } { 2 9 }   ,   y = \\frac { 1 9 } { 2 9 }"
            }
          ]
